<div class="fluid-container report-container">
  <section class="pk-content report-page report-hero" aria-labelledby="report-title">
    <div class="report-eyebrow">Rebel Defense · Legacy match 185</div>
    <h1 id="report-title">Broken Beyond</h1>

    <div class="report-board" role="group" aria-label="Final score">
      <div class="report-side report-side--myrmezir">
        <span class="report-side-name">Myrmezir</span>
        <span class="report-side-vp">14</span>
        <span class="report-side-meta">victory points · 11 of 14 sectors</span>
      </div>
      <span class="report-vs" aria-hidden="true">VS</span>
      <div class="report-side report-side--rebellion">
        <span class="report-side-name">The Rebellion</span>
        <span class="report-side-vp">0</span>
        <span class="report-side-meta">victory points · 3 of 14 sectors</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      Thirteen of you, nine from the first day, against one bot. You won on match day 22 when Novae took Begenaf and
      Dor-Valon fell. Here is how you stacked up against the Rebellion, and where it had help
      you didn't.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="pk-content report-page" aria-labelledby="report-peak">
    <h2 id="report-peak">One bot, the size of your whole faction</h2>
    <p>
      These are the numbers on day 16.6, the last reading before the bot broke (more on that
      below). The typical player is the middle player of Myrmezir.
    </p>

    <div class="report-compare">
      <div class="report-metric">
        <h3>Systems and dominions held</h3>
        <.bar who="The Rebellion" side="rebellion" value={66} max={86} label="66" />
        <.bar who="All of Myrmezir" side="myrmezir" value={86} max={86} label="86" />
        <.bar who="Typical player" side="typical" value={7} max={86} label="7" />
      </div>
      <div class="report-metric">
        <h3>Credit income per tick</h3>
        <.bar who="The Rebellion" side="rebellion" value={40_945} max={67_864} label="40,945" />
        <.bar who="All of Myrmezir" side="myrmezir" value={67_864} max={67_864} label="67,864" />
        <.bar who="Typical player" side="typical" value={5_118} max={67_864} label="5,118" />
      </div>
      <div class="report-metric">
        <h3>Active agents</h3>
        <.bar who="The Rebellion" side="rebellion" value={98} max={126} label="98" />
        <.bar who="All of Myrmezir" side="myrmezir" value={126} max={126} label="126" />
        <.bar who="Typical player" side="typical" value={7} max={126} label="7" />
      </div>
      <div class="report-metric">
        <h3>Buildings at level 5</h3>
        <.bar who="The Rebellion" side="rebellion" value={50} max={50} label="50%" />
        <.bar who="All of Myrmezir" side="myrmezir" value={7} max={50} label="7%" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pk-content report-page report-accent--rebellion" aria-labelledby="report-ahead">
    <h2 id="report-ahead">How it pulled ahead</h2>
    <p>You weren't imagining it.</p>

    <div class="report-cards">
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">272M</span>
        <h3>Its buildings were free</h3>
        <p>
          The bot's systems built and upgraded without paying a credit. Before it broke, it
          received 272M credits' worth of buildings, more than all of you completed together
          (190M). It spent about one credit in eight that it earned, and its bank grew to 180M.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">50%</span>
        <h3>Level 5 nearly everywhere</h3>
        <p>
          By day 16.6, half of the buildings in its systems were level 5; yours were at 7%. By
          the end it was 80%. It researched the level-5 infrastructure patents on days 9 to 11,
          while the typical player who bought them got there on days 15 to 17.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">L11–12</span>
        <h3>Agents bought high</h3>
        <p>
          From day 8 it hired Erased at about level 11, and every fleet Navarch it hired was a
          top-rank one at level 10 to 13. You shopped the same market, but most of your hires
          were level 1 or 2 and you trained them up. Its Erased stayed about two levels above
          yours from day 9 on; its Siderians led by about a level until yours caught up around
          day 13.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">98</span>
        <h3>And a lot of them</h3>
        <p>
          By day 16.6 the bot ran 98 agents and 26 fleets on its own. The typical player had 7
          agents; all thirteen of you together had 126.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pk-content report-page report-accent--myrmezir" aria-labelledby="report-beat">
    <h2 id="report-beat">Where you beat it</h2>
    <p>Bigger isn't the same as better.</p>

    <div class="report-cards">
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">11 of 14</span>
        <h3>You won the map</h3>
        <p>
          The sector race was tied 7 to 7 on day 14.6. You finished holding 11 of the 14
          sectors, including four that the Rebellion had held at some point.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">31 vs 14</span>
        <h3>You won the agent war</h3>
        <p>
          Before the freeze both sides ran about the same number of operations against each
          other (your 323 against its 310), but yours did more damage: 31 assassinations to its
          14, 13 seductions to its 4. Its 9 sabotages against you all failed.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">0</span>
        <h3>Its fleets never came for you</h3>
        <p>
          The bot never pillaged, bombarded or invaded a single one of your systems. Its fleets
          only fought when you came to them; it won 4 battles before the freeze, all at home in
          places like Zurka.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="report-card">
        <span class="report-card-figure">17 of 18</span>
        <h3>You hunted its settlers</h3>
        <p>
          Of the 18 battles it lost before the freeze, 17 were lone colony Navarchs you caught
          around Djullir.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pk-content report-page" aria-labelledby="report-broke">
    <h2 id="report-broke">Then it broke</h2>
    <p>
      On day 16.9 a bug stopped the bot from making decisions, and it stayed mostly idle until
      day 22. You noticed. Your Siderians seduced away 13 of the 16 commanders of the fleets
      parked at Zurka, your Erased assassinated the other 3 and sabotaged their ships, and on
      day 19 you attacked and killed all 16 of their level-1 replacements. Then you took
      Zanokha, Urqatna and Dor-Valon from it; only its home sector, also named Urqatna, held
      out. Its victory points went from 4 to 0.
    </p>
    <p>
      Who held each sector over the match, from your home at the top to the Rebellion's at the
      bottom (hover a bar for the dates). The column on the right shows who held each sector
      when the match ended:
    </p>

    <div class="report-legend">
      <span><i class="report-swatch report-swatch--myrmezir"></i>Myrmezir</span>
      <span><i class="report-swatch report-swatch--rebellion"></i>Rebellion</span>
      <span><i class="report-swatch report-swatch--freeze"></i>Bot broken</span>
    </div>

    <div class="report-strip">
      <svg viewBox={"0 0 #{@strip.width} #{@strip.height}"} role="img" aria-label="Sector ownership by match day">
        <rect class="report-strip-freeze" x={@strip.freeze_x} y="0" width={@strip.freeze_width} height={@strip.height - 22} />
        <%= for row <- @strip.rows do %>
          <text class="report-strip-name" x={@strip.label - 10} y={row.y + 14} text-anchor="end"><%= row.label %></text>
          <rect class="report-strip-track" x={@strip.label} y={row.y} width={@strip.inner} height={@strip.row} rx="2" />
          <%= for seg <- row.segments do %>
            <rect class={"report-strip-bar report-strip-bar--#{seg.owner}"} x={seg.x} y={row.y} width={seg.width} height={@strip.row} rx="2">
              <title><%= seg.title %></title>
            </rect>
          <% end %>
          <rect class={"report-strip-bar report-strip-bar--#{row.final}"} x={@strip.end_x} y={row.y} width={@strip.end_width} height={@strip.row} rx="2">
            <title><%= row.final_title %></title>
          </rect>
        <% end %>
        <%= for tick <- @strip.ticks do %>
          <text class="report-strip-tick" x={tick.x} y={@strip.height - 6} text-anchor="middle"><%= tick.label %></text>
        <% end %>
        <text class="report-strip-tick report-strip-end-label" x={@strip.end_x + @strip.end_width / 2} y={@strip.height - 6} text-anchor="middle">end</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pk-content report-page" aria-labelledby="report-players">
    <h2 id="report-players">Every player against the bot</h2>
    <p>
      Your numbers next to the bot's, just before it broke and at the end of the match. The
      small numbers in the headings point to the notes under the table.
    </p>

    <div class="report-toggle" role="group" aria-label="When">
      <button type="button" class={"default-button" <> if(@at == "freeze", do: " active", else: "")} aria-pressed={to_string(@at == "freeze")} phx-click="show" phx-value-at="freeze">Day 16.6, before it broke</button>
      <button type="button" class={"default-button" <> if(@at == "end", do: " active", else: "")} aria-pressed={to_string(@at == "end")} phx-click="show" phx-value-at="end">Day 22.6, the end</button>
    </div>

    <div class="report-table-wrap">
      <table class="report-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Player</th>
            <th scope="col">Holdings<.note_ref n={1} /></th>
            <th scope="col">Credits<.note_ref n={2} /></th>
            <th scope="col">Tech<.note_ref n={2} /></th>
            <th scope="col">Ideology<.note_ref n={2} /></th>
            <th scope="col">Agents<.note_ref n={3} /></th>
            <th scope="col">Avg agent level<.note_ref n={3} /></th>
            <th scope="col">Successful ops vs the bot<.note_ref n={4} /></th>
            <th scope="col">
              Bot's
              <svg class="help-icon report-credit-icon" role="img" aria-label="credit"><title>Credit</title><use href={"#{@sprite}#resource--credit"} /></svg>
              income vs yours<.note_ref n={5} />
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="report-table-bot">
            <th scope="row">The Rebellion (bot)</th>
            <td><%= num(@bot["holdings"]) %></td>
            <td><%= num(@bot["credit"]) %></td>
            <td><%= num(@bot["tech"]) %></td>
            <td><%= num(@bot["ideo"]) %></td>
            <td><%= num(@bot["agents"]) %></td>
            <td><%= level(@bot["lvl"]) %></td>
            <td><%= num(@bot["ops_ok"]) %> <span class="report-dim">against you</span></td>
            <td>–</td>
          </tr>
          <%= for row <- @humans do %>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><%= row["name"] %></th>
              <td><%= num(row["holdings"]) %></td>
              <td><%= num(row["credit"]) %></td>
              <td><%= num(row["tech"]) %></td>
              <td><%= num(row["ideo"]) %></td>
              <td><%= num(row["agents"]) %></td>
              <td><%= level(row["lvl"]) %></td>
              <td><%= num(row["ops_ok"]) %></td>
              <td><%= multiple(@bot["credit"], row["credit"]) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <ol class="report-notes">
      <li id="report-note-1"><sup>1</sup> Holdings are systems plus dominions.</li>
      <li id="report-note-2"><sup>2</sup> Net income per tick at that moment: the day 16.6 reading, or the first save after the win.</li>
      <li id="report-note-3"><sup>3</sup> Agents on board, governing or in school; the level is their average.</li>
      <li id="report-note-4"><sup>4</sup> Agent and fleet actions against the other side that succeeded, counted up to the day 16.6 reading or up to the win.</li>
      <li id="report-note-5"><sup>5</sup> How many times your credit income the bot was making at the same moment.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="pk-content report-page report-accent--myrmezir" aria-labelledby="report-highlights">
    <h2 id="report-highlights">Who did what</h2>
    <ul class="report-highlights">
      <li><strong>Novae</strong> took Begenaf on day 22.34, the conquest that flipped Dor-Valon and ended the match. They finished with the biggest credit income (25k per tick) and the most agents (42), and their fleets killed 23 rebel Navarchs.</li>
      <li><strong>Shareels</strong> ran the busiest agent war in the match: 242 successful operations against the bot, including 111 infiltrations, 62 sabotages and 21 seductions of rebel agents. They finished with the most holdings (16).</li>
      <li><strong>HB9</strong> landed 194 successful operations against the bot, with the most assassinations (32) and 74 destabilizations of rebel systems.</li>
      <li><strong>abdelaz3r</strong> led the raiding: 23 pillages of rebel systems, and 15 rebel Navarchs killed in battle.</li>
      <li><strong>Tianxia</strong> had the top economy before the bot broke (18k credits per tick), then conquered Vanis and Ndodo.</li>
      <li><strong>Tremes</strong> fielded the largest fleet at the end, 115 ship tiles.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="report-note">
      Built from the match's server data. "Day" is match time, counted from the start on 28
      September; the bot broke on day 16.9 and the match ended on day 22.34.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
